  - `claudepoint-hook` -> `./bin/claudepoint-hook.js`
- **dependencies**: `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@^0.5.0`, `commander`, `chalk`, `inquirer`, `ora`, `ignore`, `tar`
- **Engines**: Node.js >= 18.0.0, cross-platform (win32/darwin/linux)
- **Author**: Andycufari
- **Repo**: https://github.com/Andycufari/ClaudePoint

### 6. `claudepoint --help` output
The CLI exposes these commands:
| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `setup [options]` | Complete ClaudePoint setup (MCP + Hooks + Commands) |
| `create [options]` | Create a new checkpoint |
| `undo` | Restore to last checkpoint |
| `list [options]` | Browse checkpoints |
| `changes` | Scan for changes since last checkpoint |
| `config` | Configuration mode |
| `restore <checkpoint>` | Restore to a specific checkpoint |
| `changelog` | Show development history |
| `log <description>` | Add changelog entry |
| `init-commands [options]` | Initialize Claude Code slash commands |
| `init-hooks [options]` | Initialize hooks integration |
| `hooks` | Manage hooks configuration |
| `mcp-setup` | Setup MCP in current project |
| `check-mcp` | Check MCP configuration / debug server status |
| `uninstall [options]` | Uninstall ClaudePoint |

### 7. MCP tools exposed (9 tools)
1. `create_claudepoint` -- Create a checkpoint (optional name, description)
2. `list_claudepoints` -- List all checkpoints
3. `restore_claudepoint` -- Restore to a checkpoint (required: `claudepoint`, optional: `dry_run`)
4. `setup_claudepoint` -- Initialize .claudepoint vault
5. `get_changelog` -- View development history
6. `set_changelog` -- Add changelog entry (required: `description`, optional: `details`, `action_type`)
7. `init_slash_commands` -- Install slash commands in Claude Code
8. `undo_claudepoint` -- Quick restore to last checkpoint
9. `get_changes` -- See changes since last checkpoint
10. `configure_claudepoint` -- View/tune settings

### 8. `bin/claudepoint-hook.js`
A separate binary for Claude Code hook integration. Accepts `--trigger`, `--tool`, and `--debug` flags. It creates safety checkpoints before bulk operations and logs to `.claudepoint/hooks.log` within the project directory.

