## Step 1: Platform Compatibility

The Schwab MCP Server is a TypeScript/Node.js project that runs on Cloudflare Workers and supports local development on Linux. **Platform compatible.**

## Step 1.2: Deployment Options Extracted

| # | Option | Classification | Transport | Notes |
|---|--------|---------------|-----------|-------|
| 1 | **Cloudflare Workers Remote Deploy** | Local deployment (code cloned, deployed to cloud) | SSE (`https://schwab-mcp.<subdomain>.workers.dev/sse`) | Requires Cloudflare paid account, Schwab developer account, OAuth setup |
| 2 | **Local Development Mode** | Local deployment | SSE (`http://localhost:8788/sse`) | Requires Schwab API credentials (Client ID, Secret, Redirect URI) |
| 3 | **Claude Desktop via npx mcp-remote** | Remote deployment (client-side) | SSE | Requires existing Cloudflare deployment (#1) |

## Step 1.3: No Free-Installation Options

There is **no** `npx`/`uvx` free-installation option. The server requires Schwab OAuth credentials and Cloudflare deployment — it's not a plug-and-play server.

## Step 2: Optimal Deployment Option

**Local Development Mode** is the optimal choice because:
- It avoids the Cloudflare paid account requirement
- It can be tested locally on this Linux machine
- Node.js 22.x is available
- It uses SSE transport on `localhost:8788`

**However, critical blocker:** This MCP server requires **Schwab Developer API credentials** (Client ID, Client Secret, Redirect URI). These are financial API credentials that must be obtained from [Schwab Developer Portal](https://developer.schwab.com) — I cannot create them on your behalf.

