### GitHub Repository
**maoore/rpgmaker-mz-mcp**
- URL: https://github.com/maoore/rpgmaker-mz-mcp
- **Description:** MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for RPG Maker MZ using the `node-rpgmaker-mz` library.

### Features
- Access RPG Maker MZ project data through standardized MCP tools
- Read and manipulate events, maps, and other game assets
- Compatible with MCP clients like Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.
- Built on top of the `node-rpgmaker-mz` library

### Installation & Usage

**via npx:**
```bash
npx rpgmaker-mz-mcp --project-path /path/to/your/rpgmaker/project
```

**via npm:**
```bash
# Install globally
npm install -g rpgmaker-mz-mcp

# Run the server
rpgmaker-mz-mcp --project-path /path/to/your/rpgmaker/project
```

### Requirements
- Node.js >= 18
- npm or npx

---

### Additional Links
- **npm package:** https://www.npmjs.com/package/rpgmaker-mz-mcp
- **Blog post about it:** https://www.pulley.com/en/blog/rpg-maker-mz-mcp-server-enhancing-game-development-with-ai/

This package essentially provides an AI-assisted interface for working with RPG Maker MZ projects, allowing tools like Claude or Cursor to read and modify game project files programmatically.


